From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Doll <brektyme@brektyme.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/tc: Assume TBT-alt where the FIA is never populated

External displays behind a Thunderbolt dock never light up on Apple T2 Ice
Lake Macs, even though the thunderbolt driver builds a complete and healthy
DP tunnel to them.

icl_tc_phy_hpd_live_status() learns whether a sink is attached to a Type-C
port from the FIA, which the IOM firmware populates. On a MacBookPro16,2
the IOM never populates it at all. With an OWC Thunderbolt 3 Dock and a 4K
monitor attached, FIA1 reads:

  PORT_TX_DFLEXDPSP=0x00000000 DPPMS=0x00000000 DPCSSS=0x00000000

Not 0xffffffff, so the existing TCCOLD check does not catch it; the
register simply reads as zero, DP_LANE_ASSIGNMENT included. Why the IOM
leaves the FIA empty has not been established. Apple driving the Type-C
ports from the T2 on these machines is the likely reason, but nothing below
depends on the cause: the FIA reads zero in every state observed, with and
without a sink attached.

The consequence is that tc_phy_hpd_live_status() returns 0 forever, so
intel_tc_port_connected() is always false and every AUX transfer is
short-circuited in intel_dp_aux_xfer():

	if (!intel_dp_is_edp(intel_dp) &&
	    !intel_digital_port_connected_locked(&dig_port->base)) {
		ret = -ENXIO;

i915 therefore never touches the hardware, which makes this look like a
dead SoC-internal path. It is not. Nothing else is wrong: the DP tunnel is
up, the host DP IN adapter has completed its DPRX capability read,
GEN11_DE_HPD_IMR/IER have the TBT pins unmasked and enabled, and
GEN11_TBT_HOTPLUG_CTL reads 0x8888.

The rest of the flow does not need the FIA in this mode. With a zero live
status tc_phy_get_current_mode() already resolves to TC_PORT_TBT_ALT via
get_tc_mode_in_phy_not_owned_state(), and icl_tc_phy_connect() returns
early for TC_PORT_TBT_ALT without taking PHY ownership -- in TBT-alt the
PHY belongs to the Thunderbolt subsystem. Only the live status is missing.

So when the FIA reports nothing on an affected machine, assume a TBT-alt
sink. The DPCD read during detect is what actually decides whether a sink
is there, so ports with nothing attached still come back disconnected; they
just cost an AUX timeout per probe.

Since no HPD ever arrives either, also init the affected TC connectors for
polling rather than DRM_CONNECTOR_POLL_HPD, which is what
intel_hpd_irq_storm_detect() already does once HPD becomes unusable. That
gives working hotplug through drm_kms_helper with no userspace involvement.

Tested on MacBookPro16,2 (kernel 7.2.6) with a Dell U2718Q behind an OWC
Thunderbolt 3 Dock. On DDI E (TC)/PHY TC3 the sink is detected and driven
at 3840x2160@60. On DDI C (TC)/PHY TC1 the display also comes up on its own
after plugging the dock in, with nothing poking the connectors, confirming
the polling path.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Doll <brektyme@brektyme.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c |  8 ++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_tc.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_tc.h |  1 +
 3 files changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_tc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_tc.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_tc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_tc.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
+#include <linux/platform_data/x86/apple.h>
 
 #include <drm/drm_print.h>
 
@@ -519,6 +520,24 @@
 	return POWER_DOMAIN_TC_COLD_OFF;
 }
 
+/**
+ * intel_tc_hpd_is_unusable - Does this platform lack usable TC port HPD?
+ * @display: display device
+ *
+ * On Apple T2 Ice Lake machines the FIA is never populated: DFLEXDPSP,
+ * DFLEXDPPMS and DFLEXDPCSSS all read 0 even with a sink attached and a DP
+ * tunnel up, and no TBT hotplug ever reaches the display engine. Why the IOM
+ * leaves it empty has not been established; Apple driving the Type-C ports
+ * from the T2 is the likely reason, but nothing here depends on the cause.
+ * Everything else on the TBT-alt path works.
+ *
+ * Return: %true if TC port HPD can never be trusted on this platform.
+ */
+bool intel_tc_hpd_is_unusable(struct intel_display *display)
+{
+	return x86_apple_machine && DISPLAY_VER(display) == 11;
+}
+
 static u32 icl_tc_phy_hpd_live_status(struct intel_tc_port *tc)
 {
 	struct intel_display *display = to_intel_display(tc->dig_port);
@@ -548,6 +567,14 @@
 	if (pch_isr & isr_bit)
 		mask |= BIT(TC_PORT_LEGACY);
 
+	if (!mask && !fia_isr && !tc->legacy_port &&
+	    intel_tc_hpd_is_unusable(display)) {
+		drm_dbg_kms(display->drm,
+			    "Port %s: FIA reports nothing, assuming TBT-alt\n",
+			    tc->port_name);
+		mask |= BIT(TC_PORT_TBT_ALT);
+	}
+
 	return mask;
 }
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_tc.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_tc.h
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_tc.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_tc.h
@@ -88,6 +88,7 @@
 bool intel_tc_port_handles_hpd_glitches(struct intel_digital_port *dig_port);
 
 bool intel_tc_port_connected(struct intel_encoder *encoder);
+bool intel_tc_hpd_is_unusable(struct intel_display *display);
 
 enum intel_tc_pin_assignment
 intel_tc_port_get_pin_assignment(struct intel_digital_port *dig_port);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
@@ -7446,6 +7446,14 @@
 
 	if (type != DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_eDP)
 		connector->polled = DRM_CONNECTOR_POLL_HPD;
+	/*
+	 * Fall back to polling where TC port HPD never arrives, the same
+	 * way an HPD storm demotes a connector.
+	 */
+	if (type != DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_eDP &&
+	    intel_encoder_is_tc(encoder) && intel_tc_hpd_is_unusable(display))
+		connector->polled = DRM_CONNECTOR_POLL_CONNECT |
+				    DRM_CONNECTOR_POLL_DISCONNECT;
 	connector->base.polled = connector->polled;
 
 	intel_connector_attach_encoder(connector, encoder);
